Biometric Payroll: Staff Salary Calculation Documentation
This document outlines the core business logic, rules, and formulas implemented in the Staff List screen and the underlying SalaryEngine.kt.
1. Core Definitions & Data Sources
•
Default Hr (Req Hr): The total target working hours for the month based on the employee's assigned shift (e.g., 9 hours/day × 30 days = 270 hours).
•
Work Hr: The actual hours a staff member was present, excluding breaks and gaps.
•
Hourly Rate:
◦
For MONTHLY_FIXED staff: Monthly Salary Rate / Default Hr.
◦
For others: The specific hourly rate assigned.
•
OT Hr: Extra hours worked beyond the scheduled shift duration on a given day.
•
Paid Leave (Used Hrs): Approved leaves that are credited as working time.
2. Calculation Formulas
Attendance Metrics
•
Net Worked Hours per Day = (Clock Out - Clock In) - Break Time - Gap Duration.
•
Shift Cap: Normal Work Hr is capped at the scheduled shift duration (e.g., 9h). Any time exceeding this is automatically moved to OT Hr.
Financial Components
1.
Work Sal = Total Normal Worked Hours × Hourly Rate.
2.
OT Amt = Total OT Hours × Hourly Rate × Staff OT Multiplier.
3.
Paid Leave Pay = Total Paid Leave Hours × Hourly Rate.
4.
Allowance: Calculated daily based on presence (Present Days × Daily Allowance Rate).
5.
Deduct Hr (Shortfall) = Default Hr - (Work Hr + OT Hr).
◦
Note: This formula strictly excludes Paid Leave hours as per user requirements.
6.
Deduct Amt = Deduct Hr × Hourly Rate.
Total Summaries (Staff Screen)
•
Net Payable = Work Sal + OT Amt + Paid Leave Pay + Bonus.
•
Current Pay = Net Payable - Pending Advances.
•
Up-to-Date Total (Screen Header) = Sum of Net Payable for all staff in the selected shop up to the current date.
•
Note: Daily Allowance is excluded from the staff screen total as it is paid daily via cash-out, preventing double-counting.
3. Business Rules & Eligibility
Paid Leave Rules
•
Monthly Limit: Exactly 1 day of paid leave is allowed per month.
•
Eligibility Threshold: Staff must have 3 or fewer total absences in the month to be eligible for the paid leave credit. If absences > 3, all missing days are unpaid.
•
Schedule Restriction: Paid leaves are only applied on allowed days (default: Weekdays only, unless configured differently in the staff profile).
Bonus Rules
•
Amount: Exactly one full day's pay (Shift Hours × Hourly Rate).
•
Strict Eligibility: Staff must have Zero (0) Unpaid Absences in the month. Even taking one unpaid leave day makes the staff ineligible for the bonus.
•
Manual Toggle: On the staff card, the "Include Bonus" checkbox must be enabled to add this to the Up-to-Date Total.
Shop Closed Days
•
If the shop is closed and the record is marked paySalary = true, staff receive full credit for their scheduled shift hours for that day.
